Phase OS-20: Kernel Network Protocol Enhancements - 3 new AArch64 assembly kernel modules:

1. kernel/net_ipv6.asm (IPv6 Protocol Support)
   - Base ID: 922
   - IPv6 packet handling and address management
   - Features: IPv6 address configuration (stateless/stateful), packet header parsing, neighbor discovery (NDP), fragmentation/reassembly, extension headers, flow labeling
   - Data structures: ipv6_addr_t (128-bit address, prefix_len, scope, state), ipv6_packet_t (version, flow_label, payload_len, next_header, hop_limit, src_addr, dst_addr)
   - API: net_ipv6_init, net_ipv6_add_addr(if_id, addr, prefix_len), net_ipv6_remove_addr(if_id, addr), net_ipv6_send_packet(if_id, src, dst, payload, len), net_ipv6_recv_packet(if_id, out_packet) => len/-1, net_ipv6_neighbor_discover(if_id, target_addr), net_ipv6_stats(if_id, out_stats)
   - Capacity: 64 IPv6 addresses, 128 neighbor entries, 4 interfaces
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style (stp/ldp frame, .global exports, .bss for state)

2. kernel/net_tls.asm (TLS/SSL Encryption)
   - Base ID: 923
   - Transport Layer Security for encrypted communications
   - Features: TLS handshake (simplified), cipher suite selection, record layer encryption/decryption, session management, certificate validation hooks, PRNG integration
   - Data structures: tls_session_t (session_id, cipher_suite, state, master_secret), tls_record_t (type, version, length, fragment)
   - API: net_tls_init, net_tls_create_session() => session_id, net_tls_handshake(session_id, role) => 0/-1, net_tls_encrypt(session_id, plain, len, out_cipher) => cipher_len/-1, net_tls_decrypt(session_id, cipher, len, out_plain) => plain_len/-1, net_tls_close_session(session_id), net_tls_stats(out_stats)
   - Capacity: 32 TLS sessions, 8 cipher suites, 16 handshake states
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

3. kernel/net_quic.asm (QUIC Protocol)
   - Base ID: 924
   - QUIC (Quick UDP Internet Connections) protocol support
   - Features: QUIC connection management, stream multiplexing, 0-RTT connection resumption, congestion control, packet number space, frame parsing
   - Data structures: quic_conn_t (conn_id, state, stream_count, next_pkt_num), quic_stream_t (stream_id, conn_id, offset, fin_sent, fin_recv)
   - API: net_quic_init, net_quic_connect(addr, port) => conn_id/-1, net_quic_accept() => conn_id/-1, net_quic_open_stream(conn_id) => stream_id/-1, net_quic_send(conn_id, stream_id, data, len) => sent_len/-1, net_quic_recv(conn_id, stream_id, buf, len) => recv_len/-1, net_quic_close(conn_id), net_quic_stats(out_stats)
   - Capacity: 64 QUIC connections, 256 streams, 8 packet number spaces
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

Build all 3 kernel modules with:
  clang --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -c -O2 -o kernel/<name>.o kernel/<name>.asm

